import java.util.Scanner;

public class TempConverter {
    // Converts a temperature from Celsius to Fahrenheit and Kelvin
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        System.out.println("Enter the temperature in Celsius:");
        double c = sc.nextDouble();
        double f = c * 9 / 5 + 32;   // Fahrenheit
        double k = c + 273.15;       // Kelvin
        System.out.println("Fahrenheit = " + f);
        System.out.println("Kelvin = " + k);
    }
}
```

**Sample input:** `25`

**Output:**

```
Enter the temperature in Celsius:
Fahrenheit = 77.0
Kelvin = 298.15
```

**Variable description**

| Variable | Data type | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| c | double | temperature in Celsius, read from the user |
| f | double | temperature in Fahrenheit |
| k | double | temperature in Kelvin |

