import java.util.Scanner;

public class Interest {
    // Simple and compound interest for a deposit
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        System.out.println("Enter principal, rate (% per year) and time (years):");
        double p = sc.nextDouble();
        double r = sc.nextDouble();
        int t = sc.nextInt();
        double si = p * r * t / 100;
        double ci = p * Math.pow(1 + r / 100, t) - p;
        System.out.println("Simple interest = " + si);
        System.out.println("Compound interest = " + ci);
        System.out.println("Difference = " + (ci - si));
    }
}
```

**Sample input:** `20000 5 2`

**Output:**

```
Enter principal, rate (% per year) and time (years):
Simple interest = 2000.0
Compound interest = 2050.0
Difference = 50.0
```

**Variable description**

| Variable | Data type | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| p | double | principal amount |
| r | double | rate of interest per year |
| t | int | time in years |
| si | double | simple interest |
| ci | double | compound interest |

