import java.util.Scanner;

public class Swap {
    // Interchanges two numbers without using a third variable
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        System.out.println("Enter two integers:");
        int a = sc.nextInt();
        int b = sc.nextInt();
        System.out.println("Before: a = " + a + ", b = " + b);
        a = a + b;
        b = a - b;
        a = a - b;
        System.out.println("After: a = " + a + ", b = " + b);
    }
}
```

**Sample input:** `47 19`

**Output:**

```
Enter two integers:
Before: a = 47, b = 19
After: a = 19, b = 47
```

**Variable description**

| Variable | Data type | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| a | int | first number, receives the second after the swap |
| b | int | second number, receives the first after the swap |

Dry run for 47 and 19: a becomes 66; b becomes 47; a becomes 19.

