import java.util.Scanner;

public class Digits {
    // Digit sum and reverse of a four-digit number
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        System.out.println("Enter a four-digit number:");
        int n = sc.nextInt();
        int d1 = n / 1000;          // thousands digit
        int d2 = n / 100 % 10;      // hundreds digit
        int d3 = n / 10 % 10;       // tens digit
        int d4 = n % 10;            // units digit
        int sum = d1 + d2 + d3 + d4;
        int rev = d4 * 1000 + d3 * 100 + d2 * 10 + d1;
        System.out.println("Digit sum = " + sum);
        System.out.println("Reverse = " + rev);
    }
}
```

**Sample input:** `6829`

**Output:**

```
Enter a four-digit number:
Digit sum = 25
Reverse = 9286
```

**Variable description**

| Variable | Data type | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| n | int | the four-digit number |
| d1, d2, d3, d4 | int | thousands, hundreds, tens and units digits |
| sum | int | sum of the digits |
| rev | int | number with the digits reversed |
